# Order service

A small order service built around commands. Every command is a record, every command has exactly one handler
class, and handlers talk to orders through an `OrderRepository`. Handlers report expected problems (bad input,
unknown order, wrong status) as a failed `Result`; they do not throw.

## Commands

| Command        | Handler               | Moves the order from              |
|----------------|-----------------------|-----------------------------------|
| `PlaceOrder`   | `PlaceOrderHandler`   | (new) to `PLACED`                 |
| `PayOrder`     | `PayOrderHandler`     | `PLACED` to `PAID`                |
| `ShipOrder`    | `ShipOrderHandler`    | `PAID` to `SHIPPED`               |
| `DeliverOrder` | `DeliverOrderHandler` | `SHIPPED` to `DELIVERED`          |
| `CancelOrder`  | `CancelOrderHandler`  | `PLACED` or `PAID` to `CANCELLED` |

All handlers are registered in `OrderServices.createBus`. Commands are sent through `CommandBus.dispatch`.

An order's amount paid can be lower than its total, for example when a voucher covered part of it. Money is
`BigDecimal` with at most two decimal places.

## Tests

`java tools/RunTests.java` compiles `src/main` and `src/test` into `build/` and runs all JUnit 5 tests with the
console launcher in `lib/`. It needs a JDK (17 or newer).
package shop;

public record CancelOrder(String orderId) {}
package shop;

import java.util.Optional;

public final class CancelOrderHandler implements CommandHandler<CancelOrder> {
    private final OrderRepository orders;

    public CancelOrderHandler(OrderRepository orders) {
        this.orders = orders;
    }

    @Override
    public Result<Order> handle(CancelOrder command) {
        Validator validator = new Validator().requireText("orderId", command.orderId());
        if (!validator.isValid()) {
            return validator.failure();
        }
        Optional<Order> found = orders.find(command.orderId());
        if (found.isEmpty()) {
            return Result.failure(ErrorCode.NOT_FOUND, "Order " + command.orderId() + " does not exist");
        }
        Order order = found.get();
        if (order.status() != OrderStatus.PLACED && order.status() != OrderStatus.PAID) {
            return Result.failure(
                    ErrorCode.INVALID_STATE,
                    "Only placed or paid orders can be cancelled, but order " + order.id() + " is " + order.status());
        }
        order.cancel();
        orders.save(order);
        return Result.ok(order);
    }
}
package shop;

import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public final class CommandBus {
    private final Map<Class<?>, CommandHandler<?>> handlers = new HashMap<>();

    public <C> void register(Class<C> commandType, CommandHandler<C> handler) {
        if (handlers.putIfAbsent(commandType, handler) != null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Handler already registered for " + commandType.getSimpleName());
        }
    }

    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    public <C> Result<Order> dispatch(C command) {
        CommandHandler<C> handler = (CommandHandler<C>) handlers.get(command.getClass());
        if (handler == null) {
            return Result.failure(
                    ErrorCode.INVALID_INPUT, "No handler registered for " + command.getClass().getSimpleName());
        }
        return handler.handle(command);
    }
}
